# Hex INTEGER literals — the v0.25.0 contract (upstream #378): the C
# lexer consumes 0x/0X + hex digits itself; strtod never sees a hex
# prefix. `0x` with no hex digit after it (incl. `0x.8`) lexes as `0` +
# a stray identifier = loud parse error on every profile — the reject
# cases live in test/run.sh (reject_one asserts the C oracle refuses
# too). Byte-for-byte parity case; supersedes the strtod-parity version
# (hex fractions / p-exponents are gone from the language).
print of 0x10
print of 0X10
print of 0xff
print of 0xFF
print of 0xABCDEF
h is 0x1A
print of h
print of (h + 0x1)
print of 0x000F
print of 0x80000000
print of (0x12378086 % 0x10000)
# arithmetic on hex, precedence unchanged
print of (0x10 * 2 + 0x2)
